{"depth":"full","paper_type":"observational_alma_primary","paper_type_evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"We observed NGC 1566 with ALMA as part of a survey of five nearby Seyfert galaxies during Cycle 2: project-ID 2012.1.00474.S (PI: Nagar)"}],"fields":["nearby_galaxies","agn_and_quasars"],"question":{"value":"Do the molecular (ALMA CO J:2-1) and ionized (Gemini-GMOS/IFU) gas kinematics in the inner kpc of NGC 1566 show outflows and/or streaming inflows rather than only rotation and bar perturbations, and how large are the associated mass flow rates?","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The morphology and kinematics of stellar, molecular (CO) and ionized (\[N II\]) emission lines are compared to the expectations from rotation, outflows, and streaming inflows."}]},"targets":[{"name":"NGC 1566","details":[{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"we use the mean distance of 10 Mpc from NED"},{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"The systemic velocity of NGC 1566 is 1504  km s$^{-1}$ from H I observations (NED)"}],"coordinates":"not stated","redshift_or_distance":"10 Mpc (systemic velocity 1504 km/s from HI)","distance_source":"mean distance from NED, in agreement with Combes et al. 2014"}],"alma_project_codes":[{"code":"2012.1.00474.S","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"project-ID 2012.1.00474.S (PI: Nagar) originally approved for Cycle 1 but carried over to Cycle 2"}]}],"data_settings":[{"field":"bands","value":"Band 6","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"using the ALMA Band 6 receivers on thirty-two 12-meter antennas"}]},{"field":"frequencies_and_spectral_setup","value":"4 SPWs centered 229.415, 227.060, 241.554, 243.735 GHz; bandwidths 1.875, 2.0, 1.875, 1.875 GHz; channel spacing 1.27, 20.53, 1.22, 1.21 km/s","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"The SPWs were thus centered on 229.415 GHz, 227.060 GHz, 241.554 GHz and 243.735 GHz, with bandwidths of 1.875 GHz, 2.0 GHz, 1.875 GHz and 1.875 GHz, respectively"}]},{"field":"arrays","value":"thirty-two 12-m antennas","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"using the ALMA Band 6 receivers on thirty-two 12-meter antennas"}]},{"field":"baselines","value":"17 m to 650 m","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"Antenna baselines ranged from 17 m to 650 m"}]},{"field":"angular_resolution","value":"0.52" x 0.35" (robust=-2); 0.6" x 0.5" (robust=2)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"have a synthesized beam of 0.52$''$ $\times$ 0.35$''$ (beam PA= 13$^\circ$)"}]},{"field":"sensitivity","value":"~1 mJy/beam per channel (robust=-2); 1.2 mJy/beam (robust=2)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"The r.m.s. noise per channel in line free channels is $\sim$1 mJy/beam"}]},{"field":"time_on_source","value":"two observation blocks totalling 124 min","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"Observations were carried out in two continuous observation blocks, totalling 124 min."}]},{"field":"observing_dates","value":"June 29, 2014","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"The observations of NGC 1566 were taken on June 29, 2014"}]},{"field":"pi_or_archival_as_stated","value":"PI Nagar, own project (Cycle 2)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"project-ID 2012.1.00474.S (PI: Nagar)"}]}],"lines_targeted":[{"species":"CO","transition":"J=2-1","rest_frequency":"229.401922 GHz (nu_obs)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"CO J:2-1 ($\nu_{obs}$ = 229.401922 GHz)"}]}],"other_facilities":[{"name":"Gemini-GMOS/IFU","provided":{"value":"Ionized gas ([N II]) and stellar kinematics, program GS-2011B-Q-23","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"(*program ID: GS-2011B-Q-23*; P.I. Nagar)"}]}},{"name":"HST F606W","provided":{"value":"image used for structure map","evidence":[{"loc":"Results","quote":"running the IDL routine ‘unsharp_mask.pro’ on a HST image taken through the F606W filter"}]}},{"name":"ALMA archive (C14 CO J:3-2)","provided":{"value":"CO J:3-2 data to compare fluxes","evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"we downloaded the CO J:3-2 data of C14 from the *ALMA Science Archive*"}]}}],"external_data_from_literature":[{"what":{"value":"2-10 keV nuclear luminosity (7±3)e33 W","evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"The nuclear 2–10 keV luminosity as measured by *XMM* and scaled to our adopted distance (10 Mpc) is $\rm L_{X}=(7\pm3)\times10^{33}~[W]$"}]},"citation":"(cite: levenson2009)"},{"what":{"value":"Nuclear [O III] flux","evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"The nuclear \[O III\] flux (cite: moustakas2010) at our adopted distance"}]},"citation":"(cite: moustakas2010)"},{"what":{"value":"alpha_CO = 4.3 Msun/(K km/s pc^2)","evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"we use the value $\rm \alpha_{CO}$$\rm =4.3~[M_{\odot}~(K~km~s^{-1}~pc^{2})^{-1}]$ as suggested by (cite: bolatto2013)"}]},"citation":"(cite: bolatto2013)"},{"what":{"value":"M-sigma relation","evidence":[{"loc":"Mass of the SMBH in NGC 1566","quote":"we use that of (cite: gultekin2009) for their entire sample"}]},"citation":"(cite: gultekin2009)"},{"what":{"value":"CO J:2-1/J:1-0 intensity ratio of 1 in temperature units","evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"The nuclear CO J:2-1 / CO J:1-0 intensity ratio found by (cite: bajaja95) is 1 in temperature units"}]},"citation":"(cite: bajaja95)"}],"simulations_or_models_as_data":[],"calibration":[{"field":"casa_version","value":"CASA 4.2.1","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"Data were calibrated and imaged using CASA 4.2.1 (cite: casa)."}]},{"field":"flux_calibrator","value":"J0519-4546 (Pictor A), also phase and bandpass","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"The nearby radiogalaxy J0519-4546 (PICTOR A) was used as a phase, bandpass and flux-calibrator."}]}],"imaging":[{"field":"task","value":"CASA; moment maps with immoment","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"The task *immoment* of CASA was used to create moment (integrated flux, velocity, and dispersion and skewness) maps"}]},{"field":"weighting_robust","value":"Briggs robust=-2 (highest resolution) and robust=2 (natural)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"made with Brigg’s weighting with the *robust* parameter set to $-$2"}]},{"field":"final_beam","value":"0.52" x 0.35" PA 13 deg (robust -2); 0.6" x 0.5" PA 15.6 deg (robust 2)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"have a resolution of 0.6$''$ $\times$ 0.5$''$ (beam PA= 15.6$^\circ$)"}]},{"field":"final_rms","value":"~1 mJy/beam (robust -2), 1.2 mJy/beam (robust 2) per channel","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"an r.m.s. noise per channel of 1.2 mJy/beam in line free channels"}]}],"inherited":[{"what":{"value":"Assumed thermalized optically-thick CO (L'CO 2-1/1-0 = 1)","evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"We thus, as in C14, assume thermalized optically-thick gas"}]},"from_reference":"C14 (Combes et al. 2014)"},{"what":{"value":"Pattern speed 120 km/s/kpc used as reference","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"it uses a pattern speed argued for in C14 (based on corotation placed at the bar end)"}]},"from_reference":"C14"},{"what":{"value":"Linear bar perturbation analysis","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"based on the the linear perturbation analysis described in (cite: wong2004; fathiphd2004)"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: wong2004; fathiphd2004)"},{"what":{"value":"Modified Kinemetry with improved optimization","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"This modified version uses an improved global optimization thereby yielding results that are less affected by the starting values"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: venki2017)"}],"unstated_but_needed":["Line-free channel ranges and continuum subtraction method for the CO cube","Cell size, image size, deconvolution settings, masks/clean threshold","Flux scale uncertainty and any self-calibration","Calibrator flux density for Pictor A","Exact apertures and Gaussian fit details for nuclear spectrum decomposition","Details of the Kinemetry global optimization (modified code unreleased)","Finlez PhD bar perturbation code is not public","Coordinates of the nucleus and rest frequency adopted for velocity zero point","Pipeline vs manual calibration"],"analysis_steps":[{"order":1,"goal":"Make CO J:2-1 cubes and moment maps","method":{"value":"Imaged in CASA with Briggs weighting; moment maps with immoment","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"The task *immoment* of CASA was used to create moment (integrated flux, velocity, and dispersion and skewness) maps from the above data cubes."}]},"software":["CASA"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"robust=-2 and robust=2; 1.3 km/s channels","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"we were able to map the CO line at the observed channel spacing of 1.3 km s$^{-1}$"}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":2,"goal":"Fit rotation with Kinemetry and build rotation models","method":{"value":"Kinemetry two-pass fit (PA, inclination free then fixed to median) with six odd Fourier terms; also solid-body and ModC2014 models; Bertola model fit to stellar field","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling the Observed Velocities: Rotation","quote":"In the first run both the PA and inclination were allowed to vary with radius, and in the second run we fixed both to their median values from the first run."}]},"software":["Kinemetry"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"PA=45 deg, i=33 deg; Bertola A=200 km/s, p=1.5","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling the Observed Velocities: Rotation","quote":"The best fit parameters obtained were *A*=200 km s$^{-1}$, *p*=1.5, PA=45$^\circ$"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"m=2 modes","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling the Observed Velocities: Rotation","quote":"We assumed m=2 modes and thus use six (odd) Fourier decomposition terms."}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Residual maps compared across three rotation models","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling the Observed Velocities: Rotation","quote":"The *Kinemetry* model results in the best and most symmetrical residual velocity map for CO J:2-1"}]}},{"order":3,"goal":"Extract ionized gas and stellar kinematics from GMOS","method":{"value":"Gauss-Hermite and double Gaussian fits to [N II] with profit; pPXF on Voronoi-binned cube for stars","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"Ionized gas kinematics were obtained by fitting Gauss-Hermite polynomials and double Gaussians to the \[N II\] 6583Å emission line using a modified version of the *profit* routine"}]},"software":["profit","pPXF","IRAF"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"Voronoi bins with minimum S/N 25","evidence":[{"loc":"Observed Moment Maps: ALMA and Gemini-GMOS/IFU","quote":"to achieve a minimum signal to noise of 25 in the continuum near the \[O III\] line"}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":4,"goal":"Build pv diagrams and empirical outflow model","method":{"value":"pv diagrams with 0.2" slit; outflow velocities measured along the minor axis from brightest CO emission, interpolated and deprojected assuming in-disk outflow","evidence":[{"loc":"Observed Position-Velocity (pv) Diagrams: ALMA","quote":"The final outflow model starts with outflow velocities in the disk of 157 km s$^{-1}$ at the (unresolved) nucleus and decreases monotonically to zero velocity 2$''$ from the nucleus."}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"slit width 0.2"","evidence":[{"loc":"Observed Position-Velocity (pv) Diagrams: ALMA","quote":"These pv diagrams were extracted from the ALMA datacubes using a slitwidth of 0.2$''$"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"outflow in the plane of the disk","evidence":[{"loc":"Observed Position-Velocity (pv) Diagrams: ALMA","quote":"deprojected (assuming that the outflow is in the disk)"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Rotation+outflow model overlaid on pv diagrams at several PAs","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling Observed Velocities: Molecular Outflows?","quote":"provides a much better fit (as compared to a pure rotational model) to the inner 2$''$ in the pv diagrams at all PAs"}]}},{"order":5,"goal":"Test bar perturbations","method":{"value":"Diskfit m=2 fit to CO velocity field and linearized epicyclic bar perturbation code on exponential disk rotation curves, varying pattern speed and damping","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"The bar pattern speed ($\Omega$) and the damping factor ($\lambda$) were allowed to vary."}]},"software":["Diskfit"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"bar PA 0 deg, bar ellipticity 0.42; reference Omega=120 km/s/kpc, lambda=0.2","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"the bar ellipticity ($\epsilon=0.42$), the latter derived from our *Diskfit* decomposition"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"constant M/L for bulge, disk, bar; disk mass adjusted to 6e9 Msun (gas) or ~2e9 (stellar)","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"We further assume a constant mass to light (M/L) ratio for all three components."}]}],"fitting":{"value":"Disk mass adjusted by eye","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"in order to better fit (by eye) the model rotation curve of the CO in the inner disk"}]},"validation":{"value":"Compared model to residual map and pv diagrams","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"it fails to predict (by a factor $\sim$2) the large peak velocities seen along the minor axis"}]}},{"order":6,"goal":"Test streaming inflow with toy model","method":{"value":"Constant radial inflow of 50 km/s projected and added to rotation, compared to aperture spectra and skewness maps","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling Observed Velocities: CO J:2-1 Streaming?","quote":"constant radial inflow velocity (which we fix to 50 km s$^{-1}$ after initial inspection of the results)"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"skewness computed to 10% of peak flux","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling Observed Velocities: CO J:2-1 Streaming?","quote":"the skewness was calculated using the spectral profile down to 10% of the peak flux"}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":7,"goal":"Derive molecular gas masses and flow rates","method":{"value":"L'CO from integrated flux, M=alpha_CO L'CO; nuclear 0.2" spectrum decomposed into Gaussians; rate = mass/crossing time","evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"Molecular gas mass is typically estimated from the CO luminosity (cite: solbout2005) using M$_{\rm mol}~[M_{\odot}] = \alpha_{CO} \times$$\rm L^{\prime}_{CO}$"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"alpha_CO=4.3, D_L=10 Mpc, nuclear aperture r=0.2", v_outflow~180 km/s","evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"the velocity of the outflows in the nucleus is $\sim180$ km s$^{-1}$ in the plane of the disk, which gives a crossing time of around $5.42\times10^{4}~[yr]$"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"thermalized optically thick CO, L'(2-1)/L'(1-0)=1","evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"i.e. $L^{\prime}_{\rm CO J:2-1}$/$L^{\prime}_{\rm CO J:1-0}$ = 1"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"CO J:3-2 vs 2-1 flux ratio check","evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"the integrated CO J:2-1 flux density ($\rm 251\pm25~[Jy~km~s^{-1}]$) is 1/2.3 times that of CO J:3-2"}]}},{"order":8,"goal":"Estimate SMBH mass, Lbol and accretion rate","method":{"value":"pPXF sigma_* into Gultekin 2009 M-sigma; Lbol from X-ray and [O III], mean adopted; mdot = Lbol/(c^2 eta)","evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"$$\begin{equation}
\label{accrateeq}
 \dot{m}=\frac{L_{Bol}}{c^{2}\eta}
\end{equation}$$"}]},"software":["pPXF"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"eta=0.1; Lbol=6.7 LX(2-10keV); Lbol=90 L[OIII]","evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"($\rm L_{Bol}=6.7\times L_{X(2-10keV)}$)"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"accretion efficiency 0.1","evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"is typically taken to be 0.1"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Two Lbol methods agree","evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"These two methods thus give relatively consistent values for $\rm L_{Bol}$"}]}}],"software":[{"name":"CASA","version":"4.2.1","used_for":{"value":"calibration, imaging, immoment moment maps","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"Data were calibrated and imaged using CASA 4.2.1 (cite: casa)."}]}},{"name":"Kinemetry","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"fit PA, inclination and circular velocity field of CO and [N II]","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"We used a modified version of the *Kinemetry* package (cite: kraj2006) to constrain the major axis and inclination of NGC 1566"}]}},{"name":"profit","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"Gauss-Hermite and double-Gaussian fits to [N II]","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"using a modified version of the *profit* routine (cite: riffel2010)"}]}},{"name":"pPXF","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"stellar velocity and dispersion","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"determined by using the *Penalized Pixel Fitting (*pPXF*)* code (cite: capandems2004)"}]}},{"name":"Diskfit","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"velocity-field bar perturbation fit and IRAC image decomposition","evidence":[{"loc":"Modelling Observed Velocities: Bar perturbations","quote":"We used *Diskfit* to decompose an IRAC 3.6$\mu$ image of NGC 1566"}]}},{"name":"IRAF gemini.gmos","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"GMOS data reduction","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations, Data Processing, and Software","quote":"The data was processed using specific tasks developed for GMOS data in the *gemini.gmos IRAF* package."}]}}],"results_numeric":[{"quantity":"Inclination from CO Kinemetry","value":"33","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"deg","from_step":2,"evidence":[{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"a galaxy disk inclination of i=33$^\circ$, as derived from our CO data"}]},{"quantity":"Integrated CO J:2-1 systemic velocity","value":"1485","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"km/s","from_step":1,"evidence":[{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"the galaxy’s integrated CO J:2-1 profile is centered on a systemic velocity of $1485$ km s$^{-1}$"}]},{"quantity":"Nuclear CO FWZI","value":"200","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"km/s","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling Observed Velocities: Molecular Outflows?","quote":"double peaked profile with Full Width at Zero Intensity (FWZI) $\sim$200 km s$^{-1}$"}]},{"quantity":"Molecular gas mass in inner spiral arms","value":"6.6e7","uncertainty":"0.7e7","units":"Msun","from_step":7,"evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"the molecular gas mass in the inner spiral arms is $(6.6\pm0.7)\times 10^{7} [M_{\odot}]$"}]},{"quantity":"Total molecular gas mass in central 12"x12"","value":"1.1e8","uncertainty":"0.1e8","units":"Msun","from_step":7,"evidence":[{"loc":"Molecular mass in the inner kiloparsec","quote":"$(1.1\pm0.1)\times 10^{8} [M_{\odot}]$"}]},{"quantity":"Stellar velocity dispersion","value":"116","uncertainty":"9","units":"km/s","from_step":8,"evidence":[{"loc":"Mass of the SMBH in NGC 1566","quote":"$\sigma_{\star}=116\pm9$  km s$^{-1}$"}]},{"quantity":"SMBH mass","value":"1.3e7","uncertainty":"0.6e7","units":"Msun","from_step":8,"evidence":[{"loc":"Mass of the SMBH in NGC 1566","quote":"$M_{BH}=1.3\pm0.6\times10^{7}~[M_{\odot}]$"}]},{"quantity":"Adopted Lbol","value":"2.7e34","uncertainty":"1.3e34","units":"W","from_step":8,"evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"$\rm L_{Bol} = (2.7\pm1.3)\times10^{34}~[W]$"}]},{"quantity":"SMBH accretion rate","value":"4.8e-5","uncertainty":"2.3e-5","units":"Msun/yr","from_step":8,"evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"$\dot{m}=(4.8\pm2.3)\times10^{-5}~[M_{\odot}yr^{-1}]$"}]},{"quantity":"Nuclear outflow rate (blue)","value":"3.7","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"Msun/yr","from_step":7,"evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"$\rm 3.7~[M_{\odot}yr^{-1}]$ for the blueshifted component"}]},{"quantity":"Nuclear outflow rate (red)","value":"1.9","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"Msun/yr","from_step":7,"evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"$1.9~[M_{\odot}yr^{-1}]$ for the redshifted component"}]},{"quantity":"Molecular streaming inflow rate","value":"0.1","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"Msun/yr","from_step":7,"evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"a mass inflow rate of $\rm 0.1~[M_{\odot}yr^{-1}]$ along this spiral arm"}]},{"quantity":"Outflow kinetic power","value":"7.62e33","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"W","from_step":7,"evidence":[{"loc":"Bolometric luminosity and accretion, inflow, and outflow rates","quote":"$\rm \dot{E}_{out}=7.62\times10^{33}~[W]$"}]},{"quantity":"Total mass in nuclear outflow out to ~72 pc","value":"2.1e7","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"Msun","from_step":7,"evidence":[{"loc":"Summary and Conclusions","quote":"we find a mass of $2.1\times10^{7}~[M_{\odot}]$"}]}],"findings_qualitative":[{"value":"Ionized gas [N II] shows a narrow rotating component and a broad blueshifted component interpreted as a spherical outflow in the inner ~100 pc","evidence":[{"loc":"Summary and Conclusions","quote":"We postulate that the broad component of ionized gas is part of a nuclear spherical outflow."}]}],"claims":[{"hypothesis":"Nuclear CO non-circular motions are due to an in-disk molecular outflow rather than only bar perturbations","experiment":"Residual velocity maps, pv diagrams, Diskfit and linear bar perturbation models","result":"Bar models fail to reproduce minor-axis velocities and morphology; rotation+outflow fits pv diagrams in inner 2"","finding":"Favour a decelerating molecular outflow in the disk (~180 km/s), without excluding bar effects","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"We thus favour the presence of a molecular outflow in the disk with true velocities of $\sim$180 km s$^{-1}$ in the nucleus and decelerating to 0 by $\sim$72 pc."}]},{"hypothesis":"Ionized gas shows an outflow","experiment":"Two-component Gaussian fits to [N II]","result":"Broad blueshifted component of sigma ~140-160 km/s not following rotation","finding":"Spherical ionized outflow in inner ~100 pc","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The ionized gas kinematics support an interpretation of a similar, but more spherical, outflow in the inner 100 pc, with no signs of deceleration."}]},{"hypothesis":"Streaming inflows feed the nucleus","experiment":"Toy 50 km/s inflow model compared to aperture spectra and skewness","result":"Only some aperture spectra along the E arm are consistent; W arm inconsistent","finding":"Some evidence only; inflow rate ~0.1 Msun/yr exceeds SMBH accretion","support":"partially","evidence":[{"loc":"Summary and Conclusions","quote":"We are unable to definitely prove the existence of streaming inflows based on the kinematics of the molecular or ionized gas."}]},{"hypothesis":"Outflow energetics relative to AGN power","experiment":"Outflow mass, rate and kinetic power vs Lbol","result":"Edot_out/Lbol ~0.28","finding":"Larger than ionized-gas outflow ratios, suggesting ionized gas is a minor fraction","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"Summary and Conclusions","quote":"gives a ratio of $\frac{\dot{E}_{out}}{L_{Bol}}\approx0.28$"}]}],"reasoning":[{"field":"why_this_data","value":"New CO J:2-1 data have higher spectral resolution, sensitivity and uv coverage than the earlier Cycle 0 CO J:3-2","evidence":[{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"These new CO J:2-1 observations are more sensitive allowing us to create datacubes at the intrinsic channel spacing of the observations"}]}],"alternatives_considered_or_rejected":[{"value":"Polar and spherical molecular outflow rejected; starburst-driven outflow disfavoured","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling Observed Velocities: Molecular Outflows?","quote":"A spherical outflow scenario can be rejected as this would produce a large velocity dispersion centered on zero velocity"}]}],"limitations_admitted":[{"value":"Distance uncertain; warped or non-coplanar disks cannot be constrained; outer CO velocity field sparse","evidence":[{"loc":"Modeling Observed Velocities: Molecular Outflows?","quote":"cannot be constrained by us due to the limited resolution, the sparse velocity field, and the lack of a reliable circular rotation model for the galaxy"}]}],"referee_caveats_inferred":["Outflow interpretation rests on assumed in-disk geometry and deprojection; bar models are not exhaustively explored","Rotation model is empirical (ModC2014) and choice affects residuals","Distance and alpha_CO assumptions drive masses and rates by factors of several","Pattern-speed tension may reflect distance error or a missing inner bar","No formal uncertainties or fitting statistics for outflow velocity model"],"reproducibility":[{"field":"data_public_as_stated","value":"ALMA data acknowledged by project code; CO J:3-2 data obtained from ALMA archive","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgements","quote":"This paper makes use of the following ALMA data: ADS/JAO.ALMA#2012.1.00474.S ."}]}],"code_released":[],"missing_for_reproduction":["Imaging parameters (cell, size, masks, clean threshold)","Modified Kinemetry and Finlez bar-perturbation code","GMOS reduction details","Exact apertures and Gaussian decomposition of nuclear spectrum"],"estimated_data_volume_inferred":"~10-50 GB (one ALMA Band 6 EB set, 4 SPWs) plus small Gemini cube","score_inferred":3,"score_reason":"ALMA data public and key numbers given, but imaging settings, custom codes and many by-eye choices are missing.","rediscovery_candidate":false,"rediscovery_reason":"Recipe incomplete (imaging settings, unreleased codes, by-eye model choices), though data are public.","methods_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: kraj2006)","why":"Kinemetry method"},{"citation":"(cite: diskfit2007)","why":"Diskfit"},{"citation":"(cite: wong2004)","why":"Linear bar perturbation theory"},{"citation":"(cite: capandems2004)","why":"pPXF"}],"companion_papers":[{"citation":"C14 (cite: combes2014)","why":"ALMA Cycle 0 CO J:3-2 study of NGC 1566"},{"citation":"(cite: smajic2015)","why":"SINFONI + ALMA study of NGC 1566 kinematics"},{"citation":"(cite: dasilva2017)","why":"IFU study of [O III] outflow in NGC 1566"}],"related_projects_or_surveys":["ALMA survey of five nearby Seyfert galaxies (2012.1.00474.S)"]}
